# Scoped ignore rules for the `fish` stow package.
#
# Why this file exists: stow folds `~/.config/fish/{conf.d,functions,completions}`
# into this repository, so anything fisher (or a plugin, or a third-party
# installer) writes at runtime lands *here* and shows up as untracked noise.
# The repository root .gitignore therefore ignores those three directories
# wholesale. That is the right default -- but it also made it impossible to
# track the config files this repo actually owns.
#
# So: re-open the two directories, re-ignore everything inside them, then
# re-include exactly the files that are ours. Runtime droppings stay invisible;
# owned config stays tracked. (Note that a negation alone is not enough -- git
# will not descend into an excluded directory, so the directory itself has to be
# un-ignored first.)

!/.config/fish/conf.d/
!/.config/fish/functions/
/.config/fish/conf.d/*
/.config/fish/functions/*

# Ours: numbered conf.d fragments. Anything without a NN- prefix (fisher
# plugins, and third-party appends such as `conf.d/local.fish`) stays ignored.
!/.config/fish/conf.d/[0-9][0-9]-*.fish

# Except this one. `00-local.fish` is the machine's own configuration -- feature
# flags, secrets, whatever this box needs and no other box should see. It has to
# sort first, because 50-tools.fish reads the FISH_* flags it sets, and the NN-
# prefix is the only thing that sorts ahead of 10-path.fish. That prefix would
# otherwise re-include it via the rule above, so it is ignored again here.
# Order matters: a later pattern wins, which is why this sits below the negation.
/.config/fish/conf.d/00-local.fish

# The template for it, though, is tracked -- it is the starting point a fresh
# machine copies. It carries a .example suffix precisely so that the live file
# and the tracked one can never be the same path: editing a tracked
# `00-local.fish` would show up as a diff, and one `git commit -a` later the
# machine's settings would be in the history. fish only sources `*.fish`, so
# this one is inert where it lands.
!/.config/fish/conf.d/00-local.fish.example

# Ours, despite having no NN- prefix: `direnv.fish` shadows the identically named
# vendor snippet that Homebrew and distro packages install, which would otherwise
# hook direnv unconditionally and make FISH_DIRENV meaningless. The name has to
# match the vendor file's exactly, so it cannot take a numeric prefix.
!/.config/fish/conf.d/direnv.fish

# Ours: autoloaded functions. Add new ones here when you add the file.
!/.config/fish/functions/my_*.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/fish_user_key_bindings.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/bcp.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/bip.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/bup.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/gcb.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/kp.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/posix-source.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/ts.fish
!/.config/fish/functions/upall.fish
